# CODEOWNERS
#
# Two jobs, in this order of importance.
#
# 1. Make the customization files review-critical. Copilot reads these files and then acts on
#    what they say, so an unreviewed edit here is an unreviewed change to agent behaviour.
#    Pair this file with the "Require review from Code Owners" branch rule, otherwise it is
#    documentation rather than enforcement. Chapter 09 of the docs makes that point and this
#    file would be a poor example of it.
#
# 2. Route the areas that need domain review to the people who know them.
#
# This repository is also a template. If you copy `.github/` into your own repository, replace
# every `@ralbac` below with the team that owns that area for you. The comments say which
# concern each pattern protects, so you can map each one to the right owner rather than
# handing the whole surface to one group.
#
# Syntax: <pattern> <owner> [<owner> ...]
# Later patterns win, so the most specific rule goes last.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                                   @ralbac

# The customization surface. Every file Copilot reads or executes lives here.
/.github/copilot-instructions.md    @ralbac
/AGENTS.md                          @ralbac
/REVIEW.md                          @ralbac
/.github/instructions/              @ralbac
/.github/agents/                    @ralbac
/.github/prompts/                   @ralbac
/.github/skills/                    @ralbac
/llms.txt                           @ralbac

# Hooks execute shell commands without asking the model for permission. Treat them as
# privileged code: they are the one customization that can act on its own. In an organization
# this is the pattern that should carry a security team as a second owner.
/.github/hooks/                     @ralbac

# Environment and policy. These change what the agent can reach and what CI will run.
/.github/workflows/copilot-setup-steps.yml  @ralbac
/.github/workflows/copilot-code-review.yml  @ralbac
/.github/workflows/                         @ralbac
/.vscode/mcp.json                   @ralbac

# The fixture the labs operate on. Changing it invalidates the labs, so it is reviewed by
# whoever owns the curriculum rather than by whoever owns the code.
/examples/                          @ralbac

# Validator and its tests move together.
/scripts/                           @ralbac
